and "dome"). If this was something we talked about every day, there would p=
robably be some combination like "geo-dome" with or without the hyphen.=0A=
=0A=0ASimilarly in Lojban, I don't see why we need to have lujvo for concep=
ts that are used rarely. A tanru can work fine. There is a requirement that=
 lujvo have a specific, well-defined meaning. You could say that any lujvo =
needs to be "in the dictionary".  Do we really want to have that many words=
 in the dictionary?  Do we also want a lujvo for "Security Parameter Index"=
?  How about "Security Association Data Base"?  I think "database" should h=
ave a word, because it's rather broadly used, but not things that are this =
specific.=0A=0A=0AOn 10/28/07, Robert LeChevalier <lojbab@lojban.org> wrote=
